d to assess pregnancy-related causes"], "excluded_candidates": ["Acute cholecystitis: less likely due to hemodynamic instability but possible with RUQ pain", "Acute appendicitis: atypical presentation with diffuse tenderness and hypotension without fever", "Alcohol-induced pancreatitis: possible given daily heavy drinking and RUQ pain, but hemodynamic instability is more concerning for hemorrhage", "Ruptured ovarian cyst: plausible in sexually active young woman but hemodynamic instability favors ectopic pregnancy as higher-priority hemorrhagic etiology"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension with tachycardia (suggesting hypovolemia)", "Sudden worsening of pain during exertion (raises concern for ruptured pathology)", "History of STI and unprotected sex (increased ectopic pregnancy risk)", "Recent significant weight loss (potential iatrogenic or pathological cause)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic / Pelvic Hemorrhage", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.284, "posterior": 0.49737302977232917, "danger": 0.95, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The patient's reproductive risk factors and hemodynamic instability provide moderate support for gynecologic hemorrhage (B1), though no direct LR quantifies th…"], "evidence_against": ["Negative pelvic exam findings reduce support for B1, but alcohol use and weight loss introduce ambiguity."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic / Hepatobiliary Vascular Insufficiency", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.183, "posterior": 0.32049036777583184, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Absence of Budd-Chiari signs weakens B2, but LR+ for RUQ pain suggests weak support for this branch."], "evidence_against": ["Absence of hepatic vascular markers (e.g., Kayser-Fleischer rings) moderately disfavors B2."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Biliary Tract Obstruction", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.107, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Classic obstructive symptoms are absent, moderately disfavoring B3 in favor of hemorrhagic etiologies."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Pancreatic Acute Process", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.075, "danger": 0.7, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Exercise-induced pain and lack of postprandial pattern argue against B4, moderately disfavoring it."]}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of diffuse RUQ pain and the absence of jaundice or obstructive symptoms support biliary tract obstruction (B3) as a possible diagnosis despite hemodynamic instability?", "summary": "Lack of obstructive symptoms (jaundice) weakens B3, but diffuse RUQ pain remains a possible non-specific finding."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's history of daily heavy alcohol consumption and RUQ pain support an acute pancreatic process (B4) as the cause of her symptoms, despite hemodynamic instability pointing to hemorrhag…", "summary": "Alcohol use supports pancreatitis (B4), but hemodynamic instability favors hemorrhagic causes over B4."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of vaginal bleeding or pelvic mass on exam, combined with the patient's heavy alcohol use and recent weight loss, argue against gynecologic/pelvic hemorrhage (B1) in favor of hepatic…", "summary": "Negative pelvic exam findings reduce support for B1, but alcohol use and weight loss introduce ambiguity."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of corneal Kayser-Fleischer rings or other hepatic vascular insufficiency markers (e.g., ascites, jaundice) disfavor B2 as the cause of the patient's presentation?", "summary": "Absence of hepatic vascular markers (e.g., Kayser-Fleischer rings) moderately disfavors B2."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of jaundice, dark urine, and pale stools, coupled with hemodynamic instability, strongly disfavor biliary tract obstruction (B3) in favor of a hemorrhagic or vascular cause?", "summary": "Classic obstructive symptoms are absent, moderately disfavoring B3 in favor of hemorrhagic etiologies."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the sudden worsening of pain during exercise and lack of postprandial symptom pattern argue against acute pancreatitis (B4) in favor of a hemorrhagic or vascular etiology?", "summary": "Exercise-induced pain and lack of postprandial pattern argue against B4, moderately disfavoring it."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.44], ["B1.1", 0.3], ["B2", 0.22]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.284], ["B1.1", 0.199], ["B2", 0.175]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.24], ["B2", 0.183], ["B1.1", 0.13]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": true, "reason": "Patient exhibits hypotension (80/40 mmHg) with tachycardia (110 bpm), meeting criteria for major haemodynamic instability. Ectopic pregnancy (option A) is a time-critical syndrome requiring immediate action given sexual activity and potential for intra-abdominal haemorrhage.", "required_actions": ["Secure IV access for fluid resuscitation", "Prepare for diagnostic imaging (e.g., ultrasound) to assess for ectopic pregnancy", "Monitor for end-organ dysfunction"]}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch (B1.1) posterior (0.13) < 0.75 and dangerous alternative (B1.1 with posterior ≥0.10) remains unresolved. β-hCG results pending and ultrasound needed to resolve differentials. Emergency override active but requires further discriminators to confirm management."}, "turn_budget_used": 3, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.3, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.18254081684816678, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely the diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Ectopic implantation of a blastocyst"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Inflammation of the pancreas"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Obstruction of blood flow through the hepatic vein"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Obstruction of the common bile duct by radio-opaque stones"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Vascular ectasia within the liver"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Biliary cirrhosis', 'Abnormality of the menstrual cycle', 'Biliary tract obstruction', 'Acute pancreatitis', 'Chronic pancreatitis'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "program_faults": [], "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.44}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic / Pelvic Hemorrhage", "posterior": 0.497, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 1, "disconfirming": 1, "last_disconfirming_digest": "Negative pelvic exam findings reduce support for B1, but alcohol use and weight loss introduce ambiguity."}, "action_intents": [{"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent"